  "summary": {
    "text": {
      "en": "Triceratops was a huge plant eater with three horns, a parrot-like beak and a wide bony frill. About nine metres long, it lived in western North America about 68 to 66 million years ago, at the very end of the Cretaceous. It shared its world with Tyrannosaurus, and one fossil shows a horn that had been bitten off and later healed."
